# lsregsc.cf -- regression test for the se[j] > ctx->EPSI patch in
# prn1_coeff() (t_pgen.c). X2 = X^2 has a natural scale ~900x larger
# than X, so its coefficient's own variance is legitimately tiny in
# absolute terms despite being reliably estimated -- before the patch
# this printed "---" instead of a real standard error (rejected by a
# fixed absolute floor, EPSI1 =~ 1.49e-8, rather than a scale-aware
# one); confirmed against a real R lm() fit of the identical model.
# See lsregsg.cf/.ref for the negative control -- a genuinely singular
# fit must still print "---". (An earlier version of this patch,
# se[j] > 0.0, was reverted after it let a constrained parameter's own
# floating-point noise print as a fabricated standard error instead of
# TDA's own correct "---" -- see t_pgen.c's own patch comment.)

nvar(
    dfile = scale.dat,
    X  = c1,
    Y  = c2,
    X2 = X * X,
);
lsreg (
    tfmt = -18.10,
) = Y,X,X2;
